# Accessors are defined on the prototype under names that nobody knows. A store under a name that the class does not declare may meet one of them, so it appends no field to the objects: they would carry a slot that is never filled, and every store and read under the name would first look above it. The name is booked as stored beside the fields.
# RUN(FIELDS): link fields mechanisms=all
# FIELDS-NOT: "price" appended
# FIELDS-NOT: "stock" appended
# The twin: nothing is defined on the prototype of the other class: its late name is an appended field as before.
# FIELDS: "late" appended
# FIELDS-NOT: "price" appended
# FIELDS-NOT: "stock" appended
